description:
Design a combinational logic circuit based on a 4-variable Karnaugh map. The module takes a 4-bit input (x) and produces a single output (y) that is HIGH if any of the specific combinations of the input bits (representing minterms) are satisfied, as defined by the logical expressions derived from the Karnaugh map simplification. The output y is generated by performing AND operations on selected pairs of input bits and then combining the results with an OR operation.
module top_module(
  input [3:0] x,
  output y
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [3:0] x,
  output y
);wire w1, w2, w3, w4;
  assign w1 = x[0] & x[1];
  assign w2 = x[2] & x[3];
  assign w3 = x[1] & x[3];
  assign w4 = x[0] & x[2];
  assign y = w1 | w2 | w3 | w4;
endmodule

