Design a module that functions as an instruction read-only memory (ROM) for a 20-entry instruction set. It takes a 5-bit address input to select one of 20 pre-defined 32-bit instructions stored in the ROM. The output provides the corresponding instruction based on the address input, with a default output of zero for any invalid address. This design is suitable for use in a microprocessor or embedded system where specific instructions need to be fetched based on the program counter.
module top_module(
    input      [4 :0] addr, 
    output reg [31:0] inst       
    );

