description:
Design a bidirectional I/O interface for a package pin in an FPGA. The module allows data to be driven onto the pin when the output enable signal is active (OUTPUT_ENABLE = 1), using the D_OUT_0 input to determine the output value. When OUTPUT_ENABLE is low, the pin is set to high-impedance (tri-state), effectively disconnecting it from the output. The input signal from the PACKAGE_PIN is captured by D_IN_0, enabling the module to read values when the pin is configured for input, thereby facilitating flexible communication with external components.
module top_module(inout wire PACKAGE_PIN,
             input wire OUTPUT_ENABLE,
             input wire D_OUT_0,
             output wire D_IN_0
);

