description:
Design a memory protection circuit that generates control signals based on specific conditions of the memory address inputs. This module takes an 8-bit address input and produces 4 control signals, where each signal is derived from Boolean expressions involving different combinations of the address bits. The control signals are active low, meaning that they will indicate an 'active' state when the corresponding protection condition based on the address bits is not met. This functionality helps ensure that certain memory blocks are protected from unwanted access based on the specified address conditions.
