description:
Design a rate divider circuit that manages a sleep state based on the input clock signal. When the sleep input is low, the module resets the counter and asserts the end_sleep output to low. When sleep is high, the counter increments on each clock cycle until it reaches a value of 15 (4'b1111), at which point the end_sleep output is asserted high, signaling the end of the sleep period. The counter then resets if the end_sleep is high, preparing for the next sleep cycle. This functionality allows for a controlled awakening from a sleep state after a predetermined time period, governed by the clock frequency.
